  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Livelihoods of Unemployed (poor) Women and Youth in Addis Ababa City</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collecting additional information for programme development through stakeholder consultation, validation workshops, exposure visit to programmes in Hong Kong/China, climate vulnerability assessment, political economy analysis and Gender Analysis Research on Urban inequality in Ethiopian cities and towns (either on the impact of the ongoing privatisation to poor urban residents or on the situation of urban inequality including digital inequalities) Organise Training of Trainers course on power analysis, City RAP(Resilience Action Plan) in collaboration with United Nation (UN) Habitat, Feminist approach and on how to use digital space in the urban context Strengthening allies and networks by conducting 2 partner assessments, looking at the possibility of partnering with UN Habitat and joining the urban Non -Governmental Organisations (NGOs) network in Ethiopia Urban safety net, Covid 19 prevention and green and clean towns pilot project (?) Pilot urban safety net project focusing on towns highly affected by Covid 19 Pilot Covid 19 prevention project focusing on the most vulnerable urban households Civic Education and Social media campaign through TV channels/ radios to have a responsible youth, protect Covid 19, peace building, etc.;  Engage with social media and activists work on having green and clean (?) cities and engage 10 women activists to support the initiative.  During FY24 the project will undertake the following key activities through which about 1,500 community members will be addressed:  (1) Introduce sustainable bee feed development harmonizing with afforestation/forest management (train community members on bee feed development and afforestation, support nursery site established...) (2) Train community on early warning and disaster risk management, establish and train Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) committee at Woreda. (3) Facilitate awareness creation for communities on the negative impacts of deforestation and climate change/capacity building on partici</narrative>
  </description>
